  "question": "Does the CNBKSY root/home HTTP 412 demonstrate a site-wide institutional-IP authorization wall, or can a same-domain first-party public page be retrieved and used to recover source-emitted navigation/script contracts without querying the target?",
  "answer": "The same-domain activity page returns HTTP 200 while the root remains HTTP 412, and both expose server header ESA. The 412 body is an opaque JavaScript/cookie precondition surface with no explicit login, authorization, captcha or Access Denied wording. Therefore a site-wide institutional-IP authorization wall is not demonstrated by the 412 alone. The activity page emits /home, /signUp, /login and six scripts; no emitted search route is followed and no Zhao/Wenhui query is submitted.",
